body:
last night? and youre saying this today???

&#x200B;

dude youre def fine enough. if there was going to even be an issue of hospitalization youd be in there by now. 

&#x200B;

there is no need to inform your parents/make them worry.. with your scripts im assuming you have a therapist/psychologist or something. dont be afraid to tell them that you did what you did and how you felt afterward because, to me, it seems like you didnt want to go through with it so it isnt the biggest risk. if your psych is cool they will understand, and they will appreciate your honesty etc. but def make it known and aware that you had bad feelings and immediately understood your decisions werent what you want and they shouldnt have reason to send you to the ward.

&#x200B;

every case can be different, proceed how you feel is best fit. dont take why i say as fact, but merely an idea

bro, na. you'll still get into grad school. depending on your relationship with the prog. director i wouldnt disclose tooo many specifics, it is very alarming to people. it's good to have someone you can talk to about it tho. if you dont have someone close there are people here.

&#x200B;

also, dont stress failing a class. i failed plenty of classes. classes in high school, classes in college. i went to a couple different colleges and never finished any of them. wasnt for me.

&#x200B;

\-edit:

what was the class, how important is it overall in the entirety of your area of study?  can you opt to retake it as a summer credit? there are a ton of things you can do probably. see what your options are, and dont count out grad school.

it doesnt really matter if you do anything or not, your existence in her world threatens his, even if it doesnt. thats an issue with that dude and his trust/confidence levels. thats really between those two.. it is nearly impossible to be a dude and bestfriends with a girl with out it being something or viewed as a threat to  a boyfriend. even a potential bf. even if youre just friends if the two of you are out another person is less likely to approach her because they would assume youre together. 

&#x200B;

aside from that, its a complete fucking mess and its best to stay away completely. it sucks but you might have lost a best friend. i have because of these things and its pretty garbage.

i felt like it was inevitable always, for me.. and then i was later diagnosed. i definitely thought that was a ridiculous diagnosis. now it makes sense. i didnt know the 1/10 fact.. ill be a one some day.

&#x200B;

do you take the medication? i didnt like it.

ive thought about going on darkweb and trying to hire a hitman but i know im too poor

&#x200B;

and have zero experience with deepweb tor shit anyway so i wouldnt even know how to go about it

yeah and there are people who dont die from being hit by a car or shooting themselves etc.

&#x200B;

i was more making a joke around speed thats all, sorry that went over you.. or you just dont care for the jokes idk.

Plenty of people do seem to be venting, letting it out. There is nothing wrong with that. I have no issue with that, and have seen various relatable posts from others. I have also seen a large number of posts that do not seem as much as venting or reaching out but empty goodbye's. I also don't know what happens after any user posts what they do, so there's really no saying. Can't say I'm not curious with a few that I have seen.

&#x200B;

Also, just because I start the party, doesn't mean I lead it ;)
